The S&amp;P 500 closed at 7,723, up 0.7%, the NASDAQ composite reached 27,191, up 1.2%,

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:48.380
the TSX composite finished at 35,503, up 1.0%.

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:53.640
The nearest central bank decisions are the Fed and Bank of Canada meetings later this month,

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:56.120
with markets pricing in steady rates.

00:00:56.120 --> 00:01:00.580
Earning season is heating up with brokerage reports due mid-October.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:07.840
About 14 days ago, we picked LUV on a capacity cut tied to fuel costs and BLS energy job

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:12.080
growth confirmation, closing plus 2.40%.

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:18.000
The macro backdrop remains shaped by steady central bank policy expectations and earnings

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:19.760
momentum in the brokerage sector.

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:26.580
Looking back over the past week, TFSA contribution habits surfaced repeatedly as a theme that can

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:32.900
quietly erode long-term room if not tracked carefully. Defense contract visibility improved

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:39.580
for some names after the $20.7 billion Raytheon award, while Tello oil's Ghana arbitration

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:44.700
loss reminded investors how single jurisdiction exposure can swing results quickly.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:50.520
Valuation screens help investors identify names trading below their estimated fair value

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:53.120
based on earnings and cash flow models.

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:57.220
Today's market shows several Canadian names posting earnings beats

00:01:57.220 --> 00:02:00.220
while remaining near or below analyst targets,

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:03.440
creating potential entry points for disciplined buyers.

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:06.380
Start by pulling the latest quarterly results

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:10.200
and comparing the stocks price to earnings multiple against sector peers

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.940
using a screener on your brokerage platform.

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:19.200
For example, run a filter for TSX materials and industrial's names, with price to earnings

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:25.420
below 14 and revenue growth above 5%, then cross-check the narrative fair value estimate.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:31.760
This approach worked well in 2024, when rate-sensitive sectors stabilized after the first

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:32.680
Fed cut cycle.

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:38.540
The risk is that production guidance cuts or cost overruns can quickly erase the discount.

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:44.660
use the same process in a TFSA to avoid tax drag on any short-term gains.

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:49.560
Canadian Pacific Kansas City reached a tentative five-year collective agreement

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:54.700
with the Brotherhood of Locomotive Engineers and Trainmen covering 250 US

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:59.440
employees. The company also issued fresh long-term bonds while the stock

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:08.420
traded at $122.51. Narrative fair value sits at $139.53, leaving

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:15.180
a 12% discount. Imagine you bought shares of a mid-cap TSX name last week after an earnings

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:22.320
beat, and your order filled at $54.10. The bid-asked spread on that name went from two cents

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:28.720
to 15 cents in the first 30 minutes of trading, as volume spiked. What most retail investors

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:34.440
do not realize is that the spread widens most when retail order flow hits without institutional

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:40.300
participation, turning a small commission into a hidden cost of 1.5% round trip.

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:45.880
The professionals always check the level 2 quote and average daily volume before entering

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:46.420
on news.

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:52.180
The misconception to avoid is assuming your market order will always fill near the last trade

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:52.540
price.

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:57.940
Instead, set a limit order one tick inside the current spread when volume is below the

00:03:57.940 --> 00:03:58.760
20-day average.

00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:04.860
This dynamic appears frequently in names with recent earning surprises, where retail attention

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:05.760
surges quickly.

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:10.680
This week's simulated weekly hold targets, Canadian Pacific Kansas City.

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:13.680
The trade type is a weekly hold using shares.

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:21.360
The pick is CP.TO, Canadian Pacific Kansas City, on the TSX in the industrial sector.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:27.580
The strategy is a valuation entry after the labor deal and bond issuance reset expectations.

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:30.380
The strategy family is valuation.

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:33.640
The hold period is five sessions from entry.

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:37.120
Invalidation occurs if North American freight demand

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:39.480
falls below the three-month average reported

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:41.180
in the next monthly data release.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:45.120
The catalyst is the tentative five-year collective agreement

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:48.200
with the brotherhood of locomotive engineers and trainmen,

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:50.760
covering 250 U.S. employees,

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:53.520
plus fresh long-term bond issuance.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:05:03.500
The technical setup shows the stock at $122.51 after a one-day gain of 1.89%, with a 30-day

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:11.540
return of negative 3.36%, and trading below the narrative fair value of $139.53.

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:20.580
Risk assessment sets the stop loss at $116, representing 5.3% downside, and a maximum

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:28.740
acceptable loss of $53 on the $1,000 position. The target is plus 3% to plus 7% over the

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:34.160
five-session window if freight volumes hold. Confidence is medium because the valuation

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:39.360
discount and labor resolution align, but freight demand data remains the swing factor.

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:45.060
This trade demonstrates how to combine a narrative fair value estimate with a same-day volume

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:48.520
check before treating a post-news move as confirmed.

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:54.900
Listeners learned to require both the discount and confirming volume before sizing a valuation

00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:55.360
entry.

00:05:56.080 --> 00:06:01.080
The labor agreement covers higher wages and more flexible work rules for the affected employees.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:13.120
Last weekly hold was OSK entered at $131.73 on Monday open and exited at $134.59 on Friday

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:13.480
close.

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:20.940
The position gained 2.17% for $21.71 on the $1,000 allocation.

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:28.400
The thesis of valuation reset after earning surprise held as the stock move higher on steady volume.

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:38.080
Trade gained 2.17% while NASDAQ gained 1.2% over the same window for positive 0.97% alpha.

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:45.020
Rule. Require volume above the 20-day average before entering any catalyst-driven name already

00:06:45.020 --> 00:06:52.720
